# Merfolk Coralsmith (CR 704.5f, 700.4, 701.22): "{1}: This creature gets +1/-1 until end of turn. When this creature dies, scry 2." It enters on
# turn 1 with Plains and Forest on top of Bot1's library and nothing is scried then. On turn 3 the draw takes the Plains, and three activations make
# it 5/0, so it is put into the graveyard as a state-based action and its trigger scries 2: the two top cards now are Forest and Swamp, not
# the Plains and Forest of turn 1. Swamp stays on top and Forest goes to the bottom (an answer that does not fit the turn-1 cards would be refused).

